sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/task-containers.md): the release of a task container, for a start that failed, a group that ended, a publication or a sweep. The workflow and step names stay those of docs/cli/task/vm-release.mmd; the same name rule applies, and the intent carries `runtime: container`.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · the end of a group or a failed start
  %% kind: task_vm.slot_release
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve · Swamp Node
  participant H as Container host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the release
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the name is `HOST-tvm-N` on a configured host, and the Node records the WireGuard public key of its hub peer; the same refusals as for a VM
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-slot-release
  SW->>H: Delete the VM<br/>incus delete --force
  %%> What it does, for a container:
  %%> - `incus delete --force` in the container project: it stops the container with its nested fleet and removes its root disk, which holds the inner pool; there is no seed clone and no identity volume, and an absent one counts as removed
  %%> - an absent container counts as deleted
  SW->>HUB: Remove the hub peer<br/>wg set remove · peer file
  %%> Runs beside the step before it: Swamp starts both at once.
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>place free
    Note over GW: Delete the Node record
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the container keeps its place and its Node; the sweep releases it again
  end
